{
  "comment": "task recipe-data-b1 — the RM.Press lamp/TNT walks (Loader_Recipes_Vanilla.java:776-799 verbatim). Family expansion is the PORT-universe subset of the upstream ANY groups: ANY.Glowstone = {Glowstone, Gloomstone} (the 5 planet glowstones are the GC-compat faces absent from the port material tree) and ANY.SiO2 = {SiO2, NetherQuartz, CertusQuartz, Quartzite}. The ST.tag(1) selector legs are DROPPED — the JSON v1 row schema carries no damage/NBT faces and the configured Integrated Circuit is not expressible as a plain item id (the loom.json precedent; declared deviation: the rows answer without the circuit). DECLARED B2/POOL: the dynamite/boomstick/bullet-casing rows (Loader_Recipes_Other.java:640-669), the food-mold event rows (Loader_Recipes_Food.java:146-152) and the remaining RecipeMapHandlerPrefix generator walks (Loader_Recipes_Handlers.java:254-259 bullets, the electrode station) reference port-absent items or per-material rule walks, neither is a static JSON row face. Task toolhead-r11e-press-mortar reclaims the tool-head statements as ONE representative row per upstream walk (the mortar.json :705-706 Blaze convention): :247-250 (the ANY.Iron raw/finished pickaxe-head bases, Diamond gem / Iron base representatives) and :252-253 (the arrow retips onto the plain Empty arrows). The :251 Empty-pickaxeGem-head retip stays UNPOURABLE: upstream force-generates that head (OP.java:621) but the port force-table (GTMaterialItems.forceItemGeneration) has no landing for it (GTPickaxeGemItem head-drop CUT), and dropping the absent base from the row would be the infinite-head exploit.",
